<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-burak-grid-cell-hexagonal-attractor-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Burak & Fiete (2009), Hafting et al. (2005) & Stensola et al. (2012) entorhinal grid-cell hexagonal continuous attractor & discrete sqrt(2) module scaling — MorphoEval overall 92.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2008-burak-grid-cell-hexagonal-attractor.py` (92.6/100, up from 56.9/100 in Pass 1; +35.7 overall). The remediated script solves the 4-subpopulation (E, N, W, S) 2D FFT Burak & Fiete (2009) continuous attractor neural network PDE with shifted surround-inhibition kernels W_0(Delta_x - l*e_hat(theta)) and threshold-linear rectification [.]_+ across all 6 canonical regimes: Dorsal Module M1 hexagonal lattice (`G_60 = 1.0620`, path-integration `r_path = 0.9999`), Intermediate-Dorsal Module M2 (`lambda_2 = 54 cm`), Intermediate-Ventral Module M3 (`lambda_3 = 76 cm`), Ventral Module M4 (`lambda_4 = 108 cm`, mean scale ratio `1.4165` vs `sqrt(2) = 1.4142`), orthogonal 90 deg square non-resonant control (`G_60 = -1.0998`, `G_90 = 0.7852`), and Brandon et al. (2011) medial-septum inactivation (`l = 0, alpha = 0`) pinned-bump control (`G_60 = -0.1360`, `r_path = 0.0`), paired with automated CV segmentation of `N = 902` NeuN+ neuronal somata (`r = 0.9822`) on the Rattus norvegicus hippocampal-entorhinal immunofluorescence specimen (`rat_entorhinal_hippocampal_specimen.jpg`) and 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_088_grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor.lean`. Overall 92.5/100 (faithfulness 92.2, reproducibility 93.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 91, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor_comparison.png: rendered output of 2008-burak-grid-cell-hexagonal-attractor.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 990359 B, 2227×1863 px, artifact_sha256 9e15f015a1a8af316481cb068cc21589a23e8c95c9287f102d59cfa9d52e96bb (sha256 9e15f015a1a8af316481cb068cc21589a23e8c95c9287f102d59cfa9d52e96bb), spec_fingerprint d708b4028fb6bc24d11a5b20d2c0b94776416b67d14792a0ba60270e21d2be62. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d708b4028fb6bc24d11a5b20d2c0b94776416b67d14792a0ba60270e21d2be62; artifact_sha256: 9e15f015a1a8af316481cb068cc21589a23e8c95c9287f102d59cfa9d52e96bb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor/grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor_reference.json=951b00ff56331c34..., datasets/grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor/paper_citations.bib=e1074e8d98b9dc00..., datasets/grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor/rat_entorhinal_hippocampal_specimen.jpg=63b3a392f8d0b25f..., datasets/grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor/scout_manifest.json=77ac05875318888d...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-grid-cell-hexagonal-attractor-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Hafting et al. (2005) Nature 436:801-806 discovery of 60 deg hexagonal firing lattices in Rattus norvegicus dorsomedial entorhinal cortex Layer II with rotational autocorrelogram peaks at 60 deg and 120 deg | Burak & Fiete (2009) PLoS Comput. Biol. 5:e1000291 2D continuous attractor network model with 4 head-direction-conjunctive subpopulations (N, S, E, W), outgoing kernel shift l*e_hat(theta), and velocity modulation alpha*v(t).e_hat(theta) | Stensola et al. (2012) Nature 492:72-78 discretized dorso-ventral grid modules M1..M4 scaling by geometric ratio lambda_{m+1}/lambda_m approx sqrt(2) approx 1.42 ({38, 54, 76, 108} cm); reconstructed_in_script: 2D FFT Burak-Fiete 4-subpopulation (E, N, W, S) continuous attractor neural network solver on a 36x36 toroidal sheet coupled to a 120-step 2D foraging trajectory across all 4 Stensola modules, 90 deg square non-resonant control, and Brandon et al. (2011) medial-septum inactivation (l=0, alpha=0) pinned-bump control | Automated CV segmentation of the Rattus norvegicus hippocampal-entorhinal immunofluorescence micrograph (N=902 NeuN+ neuronal somata, 50-bin dorso-ventral laminar density profile r=0.9822, and MBP+ perforant-path fiber fraction); transfer_boundary: Normalized 2D periodic neural sheet S(x,t) on [0, 2*pi)^2 mapped onto the 270x270 cm open-field foraging arena via velocity-integrated phase Phi(t); does_not_claim: Biophysical HCN1 h-current single-channel gating kinetics or border-cell environmental wall shearing." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple environmental border-cell boundary resetting to suppress cumulative path-integration drift over multi-minute foraging sessions.",
        "remediation needed: Incorporate dorsal-to-ventral HCN1 h-current resonance time constants alongside recurrent Mexican-hat kernel width beta_m." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.25e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

